    "2": {
      "note": "Drift pruning reuses the supplied contract snapshot (or builds one standalone), lists native heads once per configured/contract code repository and observes configured and worktree branch identities. A skipped contract, failed ref census or invalid/unreadable snapshot makes removal proof incomplete: invalid snapshots are skipped and every valid snapshot is retained. Only a complete census permits removal of a valid snapshot whose repository/branch identity is absent; physical checkout existence alone is not the keep policy.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "anchor": {
